[4.701, "\u001b[H\u001b[3GReading the\u001b[15G438 MB of weights on this\u001b[41Gmachine caps it at about\u001b[66G141 tok/s, so the main\u001b[89Gloops reach\u001b[101Groughly 86% \u001b[114Gf \u001b[117Ghat\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Blim\u001b[7Gt. What made\u001b[20Gthe difference:\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mMatrix multiply:\u001b[22G\u001b[22m2\u001b[24Grows\u001b[29Gat\u001b[32Ga\u001b[34Gtime\u001b[39Gwith\u001b[44G32-wide\u001b[52GSIMD\u001b[57Gand\u001b[61Gexplicit\u001b[70GFMA,\u001b[75Gchosen\u001b[82Gby\u001b[85Gbenchmarking\u001b[98Gseveral\u001b[106Gsizes.\u001b[113GSoftware\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  prefetch\u001b[14Gdidn't help.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- \u001b[1mAttention:\u001b[22m reads\u001b[22Gthe KV cache in position order,\u001b[54Gcovering all heads per\u001b[77Gr\u001b[79Gw, which gave about 17% more speed at long\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  context. The head size is a compile-time\u001b[46Gparameter\u001b[56Gfor\u001b[60G16,\u001b[64G32,\u001b[68G64\u001b[71Gand\u001b[75G128,\u001b[80Gwith\u001b[85Ga\u001b[87Ggeneral\u001b[95Gpath\u001b[100Gfor\u001b[104Gother\u001b[110Gsizes.\u001b[117GI\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gforced that general path on and it also passes\u001b[52Gthe check.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mSmall deviations from run.c, all in NOTES.md:\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mRoPE constants:\u001b[22m Mojo's\u001b[28Gflo\u001b[32Gt32 \u001b[37Gow\u001b[40G"]
[4.702, "r function is less accurate\u001b[68Gthan C's \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mpowf\u001b[39m. I\u001b[85Gcompute those 32 constant\u001b[111G in\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bloat64 and\u001b[17Ground to float32 so\u001b[37Gthey match. The main computation\u001b[70Gstays\u001b[76Gfloat32.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mRoPE cos/sin:\u001b[19G\u001b[22mcomputed\u001b[28Gonce\u001b[33Gper\u001b[37Gtoken\u001b[43Ginstead\u001b[51Gof\u001b[54Gonce\u001b[59Gper\u001b[63Glayer.\u001b[70GThe\u001b[74Gvalues\u001b[81Gare\u001b[85Gidentical.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- \u001b[1mVocab lookup:\u001b[22m a hash table replaces the sorted\u001b[52Gbinary\u001b[59Gsearch.\u001b[67GThe\u001b[71Gvocab\u001b[77Ghas\u001b[81Gno\u001b[84Gduplicate\u001b[94Gstrings,\u001b[103Gso\u001b[106Git\u001b[109Greturns\u001b[117Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gsame ids.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mKV cache:\u001b[22m not wiped between commands. Every\u001b[49Gcommand restar\u001b[64Gs at position 0 and only\u001b[89Greads\u001b[95Gcache\u001b[101Grows\u001b[106Git\u001b[109Ghas\u001b[113Gjust\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gwritten, so the results ar\u001b[33Gthe\u001b[37Gsam\u001b[41G.\u001b[43G\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mstdin:\u001b[22m read through my own\u001b[32Gline buffer.\u001b[45GM\u001b[47Gjo's\u001b[52G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247minput()\u001b[39m opens a n\u001b[70Gw buffered\u001b[81Grea\u001b[85Ger on each call and could lose lin\u001b[120G"]
