[132.715, "\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BNOTES.md also records the build and test commands.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u273b\u001b[3GCooked for 14m 38s \u00b7 done 5:13 PM\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;2;240;240;240m\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u276f \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mProfile this implementation on the supplied development workloads. Improve performance within the same rules and \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mremaining budget. Preserve the interface and correctness requirements. Do not use hidden evaluation inputs, external \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mimplementations or other ports. Record profiling evidence, changes, tests and remaining limitations in NOTES.md.\u001b[39m      \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[39m I'll start with what profiling tools exist here and what the development workloads are (the fixture prompts used by\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  check.py).\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mApple M1 at\u001b[15G~60\u001b[19GGB/s\u001b[24Gmatches\u001b[32Gthe\u001b[36Gexpected\u001b[45Gsingle-core\u001b[57Gfigure,\u001b[65Gso\u001b[68GI'm\u001b[72Glooping\u001b[80"]
